=== qemu-arm64-static ===
DESCRIPTION ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
Linux CPU emulator (compiled for aarch64 emulation)


USAGE ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  qemu-aarch64 [options] program [arguments...]


FLAGS (24) ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
Options and associated environment variables
-h               print this help
    -help
-g port          wait gdb connection to 'port'
                   env: QEMU_GDB
-L path          set the elf interpreter prefix to 'path'
                   env: QEMU_LD_PREFIX
-s size          set the stack size to 'size' bytes
                   env: QEMU_STACK_SIZE
    -cpu model   select CPU (-cpu help for list)
                   env: QEMU_CPU
-E var=value     sets targets environment variable (see below)
                   env: QEMU_SET_ENV
-U var           unsets targets environment variable (see below)
                   env: QEMU_UNSET_ENV
-0 argv0         forces target process argv[0] to be 'argv0'
                   env: QEMU_ARGV0
-r uname         set qemu uname release string to 'uname'
                   env: QEMU_UNAME
-B address       set guest_base address to 'address'
                   env: QEMU_GUEST_BASE
-R size          reserve 'size' bytes for guest virtual address space
                   env: QEMU_RESERVED_VA
-d item[,...]    enable logging of specified items (use '-d help' for a list
                 of items)
                   env: QEMU_LOG
    -dfilter range[,...] filter logging based on address range
                   env: QEMU_DFILTER
-D logfile       write logs to 'logfile' (default stderr)
                   env: QEMU_LOG_FILENAME
-p pagesize      set the host page size to 'pagesize'
                   env: QEMU_PAGESIZE
    -one-insn-per-tb run with one guest instruction per emulated TB
                   env: QEMU_ONE_INSN_PER_TB
    -singlestep  deprecated synonym for -one-insn-per-tb
                   env: QEMU_SINGLESTEP
    -strace      log system calls
                   env: QEMU_STRACE
    -seed        Seed for pseudo-random number generator
                   env: QEMU_RAND_SEED
    -trace       [[enable=]<pattern>][,events=<file>][,file=<file>]
                   env: QEMU_TRACE
    -version     display version information and exit
                   env: QEMU_VERSION
    -perfmap     Generate a /tmp/perf-${pid}.map file for perf
                   env: QEMU_PERFMAP
    -jitdump     Generate a jit-${pid}.dump file for perf
                   env: QEMU_JITDUMP
